From a168442714da67fa12b24a6765d1c7be8a786069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:14:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] perf(sim): B2 G2 a Building floor for the cold Building
 loops, typed tier scratch
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

dense1m from load (5 runs) still had services steps of 4.3-8.4 ms without
a GC pause in them:

- the once-per-pass Building loops (prep's chunks, the stop list, the
  access seeds) ran at 1-8 µs per building on first executions and after
  Building-shape deopts, in pieces of up to 5,400 buildings (stop list at
  0.012 µs per building). params.ts INFRA_BLD_SIZING_US = 0.2: a piece of
  such a loop holds at most pieceUnits(INFRA_BLD_SIZING_US, 1, budget)
  buildings (~325 at half INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS): prep's chunk plan, the
  stop list, the access seeds and homes, shopB's block sums, the EQ / HQ
  fallback, the police scan and job sites. Chunk sizes only; the police
  scan's estimate is back at 0.03 µs per building.
- the tier engine's per-facility scratch of the current slot (facStart,
  facEnd, facSig, facSeat) were JS arrays emptied per slot and filled in
  seat order: an out-of-bounds store deoptimised allocSeats on day 25 and
  it ran unoptimised for five tier steps (up to 8.4 ms). They are typed
  arrays grown once; every entry is written before it is read within a
  slot. reachOf, splatUnion and allocSeats read the facility's id / flags
  once at their top (reachOf deoptimised ~1,500 times in 40 days on a
  later read of b.id).

Results are unchanged (b2PiecesServices; its comparison with the frozen
original skips the four scratch arrays, whose representation differs).
Exploratory runs (3, from load): services max 2.46 / 2.69 / 2.15 ms in
days 0-20 / 20-80 / 80-220 (median over runs), the worst 3.59 (prep's
first chunk on day 1).

